A RAG agent is only as good as the index behind it. Source documents changes constantly. For example, policies are revised, tickets arrive, specs evolved, etc. When it comes to RAG workloads, there is always one crucial question that needs answering from an engineering perspective: **which chunks actually changed since the last pipeline run?** Databricks' Change Data Feed (CDF) answers this question by addressing cost and sync modes. 
- **Embeddings can be expensive**: Embeddings require compute or API calls. Without change tracking, you either re-embed the whole corpus or accept a stale nightly batch. CDF turns the work into a function of change volume, not corpus size. 
- **Two sync modes**: A Delta Sync index reads CDF either on demand or as a continuous stream. 



